  "question": {
    "text": "One mole of a perfect gas, initially at a pressure and temperature of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>, respectively, expands isothermally until its volume is doubled and then adiabatically until its volume is again doubled. Find the final pressure of the gas. Given <math> <mrow> <mi>γ</mi> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>1.4</mtext> </mrow> </math>.<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0036010_Question.jpg\" style=\"width: 231px; height: 174px;\" />",
